  "remaining_integration_work": [
    "Implement and test the exact SCM_RIGHTS bootstrap transport, separately killable broker-child spawn, listener adoption acknowledgement, aggregate receipt and parent-side reap without opening a post-seal transport path.",
    "Connect the adopted listener to the frozen scalar broker loop inside that dedicated process, and make every blocking receive, ID-validation, response and terminal failure subordinate to the independent guardian-owned retirement boundary.",
    "Implement the sealed READY/release protocol over an owned local SOCK_SEQPACKET pair and prove descriptor origin, writer/reader exclusivity, one-byte consumption and lifecycle ordering rather than inferring them from descriptor type.",
    "Integrate the adapter, broker child and guardian into the frozen bootstrap, dispatcher and lifecycle closure while preserving host, input, source, cgroup, authority, core-dump, mapping and resource-envelope gates.",
    "Authenticate the successor source closure and run a separately authorized bounded Linux native qualification before any real checkpoint payload read or import.",
    "Re-run unchanged host/input/resource/real-import admission after native qualification."
  ],
